    <article>
      <div class="masthead">
        <span class="eyebrow">METHODS &amp; VALIDATION · INDONESIA IN THE GLOBAL NARRATIVE</span>
        <h1>Whose attention? Measuring Indonesia in the world's news</h1>
        <p class="standfirst">A stress test of a GDELT-derived attention, tone and theme index over
        {A.days.toLocaleString()} days. The measured signal survives; three of the four things it is
        most naturally read to mean do not. We then rebuild the headline test from the case's own
        archive and show that it changes {word(flipped.length)} of {word(af.length)} verdicts.</p>
        <div class="byline">
          <span>Demo Lab · FMV</span><span>Data through {A.vintage}</span>
          <span>{nf(A.coverage.event_rows)} coded events · {A.api_timelines} timelines</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="abstract">
        <h2>Abstract</h2>
        <p><b>Question.</b> A country-level media index built on GDELT is routinely read as
        "how much the world is paying attention to Indonesia, and how warmly." We ask whether the
        published series can carry that reading.</p>
        <p><b>Method.</b> Two independent layers over one window, {A.window.first} to {A.window.last}:
        the GDELT DOC 2.0 API's normalized volume and tone curves, and {nf(A.coverage.event_rows)} CAMEO-coded
        Indonesia events extracted from {nf(A.streamed.files)} raw 15-minute export files
        ({A.streamed.gb} GB). Every headline statistic is re-derived from the case's own published
        output; the publisher layer is re-derived from the raw archive.</p>
        <p><b>Findings.</b> First, <b>the denominator is doing most of the work</b>. GDELT's crawl fell
        from {nf(first.monitored)} to {nf(last.monitored)} articles a day
        ({pc(A.crawl.monitored_change, 1)}); articles naming Indonesia fell {pc(A.crawl.idn_change, 1)};
        the published share therefore <i>rose</i> {pc(A.crawl.share_change, 1)}.
        {pc(el.attributable, 0)} of that rise ({pc(el.attributable_lo, 0)}–{pc(el.attributable_hi, 0)})
        is predicted by crawl shrinkage alone. Second, <b>spikes are partly a news hole</b>:
        {A.spikes.weekend_mon} of the {A.spikes.n_top} loudest days fall on a Saturday, Sunday or Monday
        against {A.spikes.expected} expected, and in the median attention spike
        {pc(A.spikes.denom_median, 0)} of the move is a smaller world crawl rather than more Indonesia
        coverage. The Kanjuruhan stadium disaster passes the attention gate at
        {kanjA.ratio.toFixed(2)}× on a numerator that moved {kanjA.numer.toFixed(2)}×. Third,
        <b>the "global" narrative is mostly domestic</b>: {pub.indonesian_in_top25} of the
        {pub.top.length} largest publishers are based in Indonesia, Indonesian outlets carry
        {pc(attr.origin_by_year[0].indonesia_share, 0)} of the archive in {attr.origin_by_year[0].year}
        rising to {pc(attr.origin_by_year[attr.origin_by_year.length - 1].indonesia_share, 0)} by
        {attr.origin_by_year[attr.origin_by_year.length - 1].year}, and the state wire alone is
        {pc(pub.state_share, 1)} of everything. Fourth, <b>rebuilding the anchor test on foreign
        publishers only changes {word(flipped.length)} of {word(af.length)} verdicts</b>: the disaster
        that passes turns into a {kanj.foreign.ratio.toFixed(2)}× <i>fall</i>, while {word(missed.length)}
        events the case records as failing show foreign spikes of
        {Math.min(...missed.map((m: any) => m.foreign.ratio)).toFixed(1)}–{Math.max(...missed.map((m: any) => m.foreign.ratio)).toFixed(1)}×.
        Fifth, <b>the tone rise is two-thirds real</b>: an exact decomposition splits the
        {sg(dec.delta, 2)}-point warming into {sg(dec.within, 2)} from the same outlets and
        {sg(composition, 2)} from a change in which outlets GDELT reads.</p>
        <p><b>Conclusion.</b> The instrument measures <i>what is being said about Indonesia and by whom</i>
        well, and <i>how much the world is looking</i> badly. Its level series should be withdrawn as a
        measure of global attention and republished as two: a composition series, which is sound, and a
        foreign-attention series, which the archive can already produce and which disagrees with the
        published one in both directions.</p>
      </section>

